### RxCare API - run requests from VS Code with the "REST Client" extension.
### Click "Send Request" above each request. Start the app first (Tasks: App: start).

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### Health check (no login needed)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/health

### Sign in as pharmacist - the token is reused by the requests below
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "rph.jones", "password": "Pharm@123" }

###
@token = {{login.response.body.token}}

### Dashboard summary
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/dashboard
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### All patients
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/patients
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Low-stock drugs
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/inventory/low-stock
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Prescriptions waiting for verification
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/prescriptions?status=NEW
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Allergy check: John Carter (patient 1) is allergic to PENICILLIN -> expect 422 ALLERGY_CONFLICT
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/prescriptions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "patientId": 1, "ndc": "50000-0101-01", "prescriber": "Dr. Demo", "sig": "Take 1 capsule three times daily",
  "quantity": 30, "daysSupply": 10, "refills": 0 }

### Create a valid prescription (Lisinopril for patient 3) -> expect 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/prescriptions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "patientId": 3, "ndc": "50000-0202-01", "prescriber": "Dr. Demo", "sig": "Take 1 tablet once daily",
  "quantity": 30, "daysSupply": 30, "refills": 2 }
